     tooltip = "จำนวนแท่งซ้าย / ขวาที่ใช้ยืนยันจุด Low / High\nป้ายจะขึ้นหลังจุดนั้น right แท่ง (3 แท่งบน 5m = 15 นาที) ค่าน้อย = เร็วขึ้นแต่หลอกบ่อยขึ้น")
int    divMax      = input.int(60, "Max bars between the 2 points", minval = 10, maxval = 200, group = G_DIV)
bool   divZone     = input.bool(true, "Only from RSI below", inline = "dz", group = G_DIV)
int    divLo       = input.int(40, "", minval = 1, maxval = 50, inline = "dz", group = G_DIV)
int    divHi       = input.int(60, "/ above", minval = 50, maxval = 99, inline = "dz", group = G_DIV,
     tooltip = "กรองเฉพาะ divergence ที่จุดแรกของ RSI อยู่ในโซนขายมาก / ซื้อมาก (Bull: RSI จุดแรก ≤ 40, Bear: RSI จุดแรก ≥ 60) ลดสัญญาณระหว่างที่ราคาแกว่งกลาง ๆ\nปิดเพื่อแสดงทุก divergence")
bool   alDiv       = input.bool(false, "RSI divergence", group = G_ALRT,
     tooltip = "แจ้งเตือนเมื่อเกิด Bull / Bear RSI divergence บน TF ที่ตั้ง Alert (5m) แจ้งตอนแท่งปิด")

// Effective HTFs (fixed set, auto by chart TF, or manual)
int    chartS   = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)
bool   fixedSet = tfMode == "5m · 15m · 1H · 4H · 1D"
bool   autoSet  = tfMode == "Auto by chart TF"
string eTf1     = fixedSet ? "5" : autoSet ? (chartS <= 60 ? "5" : chartS <= 300 ? "15" : chartS <= 900 ? "60" : chartS <= 3600 ? "240" : "D") : tf1
string eTf2     = fixedSet ? "15" : autoSet ? (chartS <= 60 ? "15" : chartS <= 300 ? "60" : chartS <= 900 ? "240" : chartS <= 3600 ? "D" : "W") : tf2
string eTf3     = fixedSet ? "60" : autoSet ? (chartS <= 60 ? "60" : chartS <= 300 ? "240" : chartS <= 900 ? "D" : chartS <= 3600 ? "W" : "M") : tf3
string eTf4     = fixedSet ? "240" : tf4
string eTf5     = fixedSet ? "D" : tf5
bool   eUse1    = fixedSet or autoSet or useTF1
bool   eUse2    = fixedSet or autoSet or useTF2
bool   eUse3    = fixedSet or autoSet or useTF3
bool   eUse4    = fixedSet or (not autoSet and useTF4)
bool   eUse5    = fixedSet or (not autoSet and useTF5)

float  atrC    = ta.atr(14)

// History window for structure / liquidity drawings
int    histCut = timenow - histDays * 86400000
bool   histOk  = histDays == 0 or time >= histCut
var array<line>  histLines  = array.new<line>()
var array<label> histLabels = array.new<label>()
string lblSize = lblSizeOpt == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : lblSizeOpt == "Small" ? size.small : size.normal

//==============================================================================
// TYPES
//==============================================================================
type Zone
    box    bx
    float  top
    float  bot
    int    left
    bool   bull
    bool   isOB
    color  col
    int    rank        // 0 = chart TF, 1..5 = HTF slot (higher = more important)
    string tag         // timeframe name, e.g. "4H"
    string lbl         // base label text, e.g. "OB 4H"
    int    born        // chart bar_index when the zone was drawn
    int    tfSec       // timeframe of the zone in seconds (for alerts)
    line   ce          // 50% line (na when off)
    int    bdT         // border transparency (higher TF = lighter)
    bool   mitigated = false
    bool   entered   = false   // price has traded into the zone at least once
    bool   armed     = false   // price has been farther away than the approach distance
    bool   near      = false   // approach alert already sent

//==============================================================================
// DETECTION (runs on any timeframe, also inside request.security)
//==============================================================================
// Returns: bull OB [flag, top, bottom, time], bear OB [...], bull FVG [...], bear FVG [...],
//          structure (1 = bull BOS, 2 = bull CHoCH, -1 = bear BOS, -2 = bear CHoCH),
//          broken level, broken level time, trend (1 / -1 / 0),
//          flip level (swing a close must break to turn the trend, na if none yet)
detect(int len, float minPct) =>
    var float swH      = na
    var int   swHBar   = na
    var int   swHTime  = na
    var bool  swHUsed  = true
    var float swL      = na
    var int   swLBar   = na
    var int   swLTime  = na
    var bool  swLUsed  = true
    var int   trend    = 0

    float atr = ta.atr(14)
    float cap = obMaxAtr * atr
    float ph  = ta.pivothigh(high, len, len)
    float pl  = ta.pivotlow(low, len, len)
    if not na(ph)
        swH     := ph
        swHBar  := bar_index - len
        swHTime := time[len]
        swHUsed := false
    if not na(pl)
        swL     := pl
        swLBar  := bar_index - len
        swLTime := time[len]
        swLUsed := false

    bool  bullOB  = false
    float bullOBT = na
    float bullOBB = na
    int   bullOBX = na
    bool  bearOB  = false
    float bearOBT = na
    float bearOBB = na
    int   bearOBX = na
    int   ms      = 0
    float msLvl   = na
    int   msX     = na

    // Bullish break of structure -> Order Block = candle with lowest low of the leg
    if not swHUsed and close > swH
        swHUsed := true
        ms      := trend < 0 ? 2 : 1
        msLvl   := swH
        msX     := swHTime
        trend   := 1
        int   span = math.max(1, math.min(bar_index - swHBar, 300))
        float mn   = low[1]
        int   idx  = 1
        for i = 1 to span
            if low[i] < mn
                mn  := low[i]
                idx := i
        bullOB  := true
        bullOBT := high[idx]
        bullOBB := low[idx]
        bullOBX := time[idx]
        // Oversized OB: keep the upper part (closest to price) or skip it
        if obMaxAtr > 0 and bullOBT - bullOBB > cap
            if obSizeMode == "Skip"
                bullOB := false
            else
                bullOBB := bullOBT - cap

    // Bearish break of structure -> Order Block = candle with highest high of the leg
    if not swLUsed and close < swL
        swLUsed := true
        ms      := trend > 0 ? -2 : -1
        msLvl   := swL
        msX     := swLTime
        trend   := -1
        int   span = math.max(1, math.min(bar_index - swLBar, 300))
        float mx   = high[1]
        int   idx  = 1
        for i = 1 to span
            if high[i] > mx
                mx  := high[i]
                idx := i
        bearOB  := true
        bearOBT := high[idx]
        bearOBB := low[idx]
        bearOBX := time[idx]
        // Oversized OB: keep the lower part (closest to price) or skip it
        if obMaxAtr > 0 and bearOBT - bearOBB > cap
            if obSizeMode == "Skip"
                bearOB := false
            else
                bearOBT := bearOBB + cap

    // Fair Value Gaps (3-candle imbalance)
    bool bullFVG = low > high[2] and close[1] > high[2] and (low - high[2]) / close * 100 >= minPct
    bool bearFVG = high < low[2] and close[1] < low[2] and (low[2] - high) / close * 100 >= minPct

    float flip = trend > 0 ? (swLUsed ? na : swL) : trend < 0 ? (swHUsed ? na : swH) : na

    [bullOB, bullOBT, bullOBB, bullOBX,
     bearOB, bearOBT, bearOBB, bearOBX,
     bullFVG, low, high[2], time[2],
     bearFVG, low[2], high, time[2],
     ms, msLvl, msX, trend, flip]

// Same as detect() but shifted one bar back -> used with lookahead_on for non-repainting HTF data
// (also returns that bar's close, used to invalidate HTF Order Blocks in Close mode)
detectConfirmed(int len, float minPct) =>
    [a1, a2, a3, a4, b1, b2, b3, b4, c1, c2, c3, c4, d1, d2, d3, d4, m1, m2, m3, t, f] = detect(len, minPct)
    [a1[1], a2[1], a3[1], a4[1], b1[1], b2[1], b3[1], b4[1], c1[1], c2[1], c3[1], c4[1], d1[1], d2[1], d3[1], d4[1], m1[1], m2[1], m3[1], t[1], f[1], close[1]]

// Only the structure break of the last confirmed bar (for CHoCH / BOS of a higher timeframe)
structConfirmed(int len) =>
    [a1, a2, a3, a4, b1, b2, b3, b4, c1, c2, c3, c4, d1, d2, d3, d4, m1, m2, m3, t, f] = detect(len, 0.0)
    [m1[1], m2[1], m3[1]]

//==============================================================================
// HELPERS
//==============================================================================
tfName(simple string tf) =>
    int s = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    s >= 2592000 and s % 2592000 == 0 ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 2592000)) + "M" :
     s >= 604800 and s % 604800 == 0  ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 604800)) + "W" :
     s >= 86400 and s % 86400 == 0    ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 86400)) + "D" :
     s >= 3600 and s % 3600 == 0      ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 3600)) + "H" :
     s >= 60                          ? str.tostring(math.round(s / 60)) + "m" : str.tostring(s) + "s"

sameKind(Zone a, bool bull, bool isOB) => a.bull == bull and a.isOB == isOB

// Delete a zone's drawings
killZone(Zone z) =>
    z.bx.delete()
    line.delete(z.ce)

addZone(array<Zone> zs, float top, float bot, int t, bool bull, bool isOB, color c, int rank, string tag, int maxN, int tfSec) =>
    // A newer OB replaces an overlapping older OB of the same TF (FVGs are kept separately)
    int n = zs.size()
    if isOB and n > 0
        for i = n - 1 to 0
            Zone z = zs.get(i)
            if not z.mitigated and sameKind(z, bull, isOB) and z.top >= bot and z.bot <= top
                zs.remove(i)
                killZone(z)
    // Higher timeframes are drawn lighter so big zones do not hide the candles
    int   fillT = not fadeHTF ? int(color.t(c)) : tfSec >= 86400 ? 94 : tfSec >= 14400 ? 88 : int(color.t(c))
    int   bdT   = not fadeHTF ? 30 : tfSec >= 86400 ? 60 : tfSec >= 14400 ? 45 : 30
    color fc    = color.new(c, fillT)
    string lbl  = (isOB ? "OB" : "FVG") + (rank > 0 ? " " + tag : "")
    box bx = box.new(t, top, time, bot, xloc = xloc.bar_time, extend = extend.right,
         border_color = color.new(c, bdT), border_style = rank > 0 ? line.style_dashed : line.style_solid,
         bgcolor = fc, text = lbl, text_size = lblSize, text_color = color.new(c, 0),
         text_halign = text.align_right, text_valign = rank > 0 ? text.align_top : text.align_bottom)
    line ce = showCE ? line.new(t, (top + bot) / 2, time, (top + bot) / 2, xloc = xloc.bar_time, extend = extend.right,
         color = color.new(c, bdT), style = line.style_dotted) : na
    zs.unshift(Zone.new(bx, top, bot, t, bull, isOB, fc, rank, tag, lbl, bar_index, tfSec, ce, bdT))
    // Keep at most maxN zones of this kind (newest first)
    array<int> drop = array.new<int>()
    int cnt = 0
    for i = 0 to zs.size() - 1
        if sameKind(zs.get(i), bull, isOB)
            cnt += 1
            if cnt > maxN
                drop.push(i)
    int d = drop.size()
    if d > 0
        for j = d - 1 to 0
            Zone old = zs.remove(drop.get(j))
            killZone(old)

// Mitigation check (confirmed bars). OBs in Close mode are checked against the close of their own timeframe:
// obCheck = a bar of that timeframe just closed, obClose = its close (chart TF: every bar, close)
updateZones(array<Zone> zs, bool obCheck, float obClose) =>
    int n = zs.size()
    if n > 0
        for i = n - 1 to 0
            Zone z = zs.get(i)
            if not z.mitigated
                bool hit = z.isOB ?
                     (obMitMode == "Close" ? obCheck and (z.bull ? obClose < z.bot : obClose > z.top) : (z.bull ? low < z.bot : high > z.top)) :
                     (z.bull ? low <= z.bot : high >= z.top)
                if hit
                    z.mitigated := true
                    if hideMit
                        zs.remove(i)
                        killZone(z)
                    else
                        z.bx.set_extend(extend.none)
                        z.bx.set_right(time)
                        z.bx.set_bgcolor(color.new(chart.fg_color, 92))
                        z.bx.set_border_color(color.new(chart.fg_color, 80))
                        z.bx.set_text_color(color.new(chart.fg_color, 60))
                        line.delete(z.ce)
                else if fvgShrink and not z.isOB and (bar_index > z.born or z.rank > 0) and (z.bull ? low < z.top : high > z.bot)
                    // Partially filled FVG: keep only the part of the gap that is still open
                    if z.bull
                        z.top := low
                        z.bx.set_top(low)
                    else
                        z.bot := high
                        z.bx.set_bottom(high)
                    if showCE
                        float mid = (z.top + z.bot) / 2
                        z.ce.set_y1(mid)
                        z.ce.set_y2(mid)
    n

fmt(float p) => str.tostring(p, format.mintick)
// Short price text (1 decimal for prices like gold) for the dashboard and distances
fmtS(float p) => close >= 1000 ? str.tostring(p, "#.0") : fmt(p)

tfOk(int sec) => (sec == 300 and al5) or (sec == 900 and al15) or (sec == 3600 and al60) or (sec == 14400 and al240) or (sec == 86400 and alD)

joinMsg(string a, string b) => a == "" ? b : b == "" ? a : a + " | " + b

// Notification events: a key (so each event is sent once) and its text, collected during the script run
pushEv(array<string> evK, array<string> evT, string k, string t) =>
    evK.push(k)
    evT.push(t)

zoneKey(Zone z) => str.tostring(z.left) + z.tag + (z.isOB ? "O" : "F") + (z.bull ? "u" : "d")
zoneTxt(Zone z) => (z.bull ? "Bullish " : "Bearish ") + (z.isOB ? "OB " : "FVG ") + z.tag + " " + fmt(z.bot) + "–" + fmt(z.top)

// First time price trades into a zone (once per zone, also intrabar on realtime bars).
// HTF zones count from the chart bar they appear on (that bar comes after the HTF bar that formed them).
// Returns [bullish entered, bearish entered] for the alert-enabled TFs and zone types.
checkEntry(array<Zone> zs, array<string> evK, array<string> evT) =>
    bool bIn = false
    bool sIn = false
    for z in zs
        if not z.mitigated and not z.entered and (bar_index > z.born or z.rank > 0) and high >= z.bot and low <= z.top
            z.entered := true
            if tfOk(z.tfSec) and (z.isOB ? alOB : alFVG)
                bIn := bIn or z.bull
                sIn := sIn or not z.bull
                if alEnter
                    pushEv(evK, evT, "E" + zoneKey(z), "entered " + zoneTxt(z))
    [bIn, sIn]

// Price coming within nearAtr x ATR of a 1H+ zone it has not reached yet.
// Once per zone, and only after price was farther away (a zone born next to price does not alert at once).
checkNear(array<Zone> zs, array<string> evK, array<string> evT) =>
    float thr = nearAtr * atrC
    int   cnt = 0
    for z in zs
        if not z.mitigated and not z.entered and not z.near and z.tfSec >= 3600 and tfOk(z.tfSec) and (z.isOB ? alOB : alFVG)
            float d = z.bull ? low - z.top : z.bot - high
            if d > thr
                z.armed := true
            else if z.armed and d > 0
                z.near := true
                cnt    += 1
                pushEv(evK, evT, "N" + zoneKey(z), "approaching " + zoneTxt(z) + " (" + fmtS(z.bull ? close - z.top : z.bot - close) + " away)")
    cnt

// Trend of a 1H / 4H slot flipped on this bar (its first chart bar after the HTF close)
trendFlipMsg(simple string tf, bool valid, int t, float f) =>
    int   tPrev = t[1]
    float fPrev = f[1]
    int   s     = timeframe.in_seconds(tf)
    string msg  = ""
    if valid and (s == 3600 or s == 14400) and t != 0 and tPrev != 0 and t != tPrev
        msg := tfName(tf) + " trend turned " + (t > 0 ? "Bullish" : "Bearish") +
             (na(fPrev) ? "" : (t > 0 ? " (closed above " : " (closed below ") + fmtS(fPrev) + ")")
    msg

// Creates zones for one timeframe, returns [newBullOB, newBearOB, newBullFVG, newBearFVG]
handleZones(bool isNew, int rank, string tag, int tfSec, array<Zone> zs,
     bool a1, float a2, float a3, int a4, bool b1, float b2, float b3, int b4,
     bool c1, float c2, float c3, int c4, bool d1, float d2, float d3, int d4, array<string> evK, array<string> evT) =>
    bool nbOB = isNew and showOB and a1
    bool nsOB = isNew and showOB and b1
    bool nbF  = isNew and showFVG and c1
    bool nsF  = isNew and showFVG and d1
    if nbOB
        addZone(zs, a2, a3, a4, true, true, bullOBCol, rank, tag, maxOB, tfSec)
        if alNew
            pushEv(evK, evT, "Z" + str.tostring(a4) + tag + "Ou", "new Bullish OB " + tag + " " + fmt(a3) + "–" + fmt(a2))
    if nsOB
        addZone(zs, b2, b3, b4, false, true, bearOBCol, rank, tag, maxOB, tfSec)
        if alNew
            pushEv(evK, evT, "Z" + str.tostring(b4) + tag + "Od", "new Bearish OB " + tag + " " + fmt(b3) + "–" + fmt(b2))
    if nbF
        addZone(zs, c2, c3, c4, true, false, bullFVGCol, rank, tag, maxFVG, tfSec)
        if alNew
            pushEv(evK, evT, "Z" + str.tostring(c4) + tag + "Fu", "new Bullish FVG " + tag + " " + fmt(c3) + "–" + fmt(c2))
    if nsF
        addZone(zs, d2, d3, d4, false, false, bearFVGCol, rank, tag, maxFVG, tfSec)
        if alNew
            pushEv(evK, evT, "Z" + str.tostring(d4) + tag + "Fd", "new Bearish FVG " + tag + " " + fmt(d3) + "–" + fmt(d2))
    [nbOB, nsOB, nbF, nsF]

// Higher-timeframe slot (non-repainting: only confirmed HTF bars are used)
var int chartSec = timeframe.in_seconds(timeframe.period)

htfSlot(simple string tf, bool use, array<Zone> zs, int rank, array<string> evK, array<string> evT) =>
    [a1, a2, a3, a4, b1, b2, b3, b4, c1, c2, c3, c4, d1, d2, d3, d4, m1, m2, m3, t, f, hc] =
         request.security(syminfo.tickerid, tf, detectConfirmed(swingLen, fvgMinPct), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
    bool valid = use and timeframe.in_seconds(tf) > chartSec
    bool isNew = valid and timeframe.change(tf)
    [nb, ns, nbf, nsf] = handleZones(isNew, rank, tfName(tf), timeframe.in_seconds(tf), zs,
         a1, a2, a3, a4, b1, b2, b3, b4, c1, c2, c3, c4, d1, d2, d3, d4, evK, evT)
    [valid, t, f, nb or nbf, ns or nsf, isNew, hc]

//==============================================================================
// STATE
//==============================================================================
var array<Zone> zC  = array.new<Zone>()
var array<Zone> zH1 = array.new<Zone>()
var array<Zone> zH2 = array.new<Zone>()
var array<Zone> zH3 = array.new<Zone>()
var array<Zone> zH4 = array.new<Zone>()
var array<Zone> zH5 = array.new<Zone>()

//==============================================================================
// DISPLAY FILTER (nearest zones + higher-TF priority)
//==============================================================================
collect(array<Zone> src, array<Zone> dst) =>
    for z in src
        if not z.mitigated
            dst.push(z)

setVisible(Zone z, bool vis, string extra) =>
    z.bx.set_bgcolor(vis ? z.col : color(na))
    z.bx.set_border_color(vis ? color.new(z.col, z.bdT) : color(na))
    z.bx.set_text_color(vis ? color.new(z.col, 0) : color(na))
    z.bx.set_text(z.lbl + extra)
    if showCE
        z.ce.set_color(vis ? color.new(z.col, z.bdT) : color(na))

refreshDisplay() =>
    array<Zone> pool = array.new<Zone>()
    collect(zC, pool)
    collect(zH1, pool)
    collect(zH2, pool)
    collect(zH3, pool)
    collect(zH4, pool)
    collect(zH5, pool)
    int n = pool.size()
    if n > 0
        array<bool>   hid   = array.new<bool>(n, false)
        array<string> extra = array.new<string>(n, "")
        // Lower-TF zone inside a higher-TF zone of the same kind -> show only the higher one (confluence label)
        if mergeTF
            for i = 0 to n - 1
                Zone a = pool.get(i)
                for j = 0 to n - 1
                    Zone b = pool.get(j)
                    if b.rank > a.rank and sameKind(b, a.bull, a.isOB) and b.top >= a.bot and b.bot <= a.top
                        hid.set(i, true)
                        if not str.contains(extra.get(j) + "+", "+" + a.tag + "+")
                            extra.set(j, extra.get(j) + "+" + a.tag)
                        break
        // Nearest N per side and type
        array<float> dist = array.new<float>(n, 0.0)
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            Zone z = pool.get(i)
            dist.set(i, z.bull ? math.max(0.0, close - z.top) : math.max(0.0, z.bot - close))
        array<int> ord = dist.sort_indices(order.ascending)
        array<int> cnt = array.new<int>(4, 0)
        for i in ord
            Zone z = pool.get(i)
            bool vis = not hid.get(i)
            if vis and nearestOnly
                int k = (z.isOB ? 0 : 2) + (z.bull ? 0 : 1)
                if cnt.get(k) >= nearestN
                    vis := false
                else
                    cnt.set(k, cnt.get(k) + 1)
            setVisible(z, vis, extra.get(i))

//==============================================================================
// MAIN
//==============================================================================
// Notification events of this script run (sent together at the end of the script)
array<string> evKey = array.new<string>()
array<string> evTxt = array.new<string>()

// Chart-TF mitigation first, so zones created on this bar are not mitigated by the bar that formed them
if barstate.isconfirmed
    updateZones(zC, true, close)

// Chart timeframe
string chartTag = tfName(timeframe.period)
[ca1, ca2, ca3, ca4, cb1, cb2, cb3, cb4, cc1, cc2, cc3, cc4, cd1, cd2, cd3, cd4, cms, cmsLvl, cmsX, cTrend, cFlip] = detect(swingLen, fvgMinPct)
[cnb, cns, cnbf, cnsf] = handleZones(showChartTF and barstate.isconfirmed, 0, chartTag, chartSec, zC,
     ca1, ca2, ca3, ca4, cb1, cb2, cb3, cb4, cc1, cc2, cc3, cc4, cd1, cd2, cd3, cd4, evKey, evTxt)

// Higher timeframes
[v1, t1, f1, nBull1, nBear1, new1, hc1] = htfSlot(eTf1, eUse1, zH1, 1, evKey, evTxt)
[v2, t2, f2, nBull2, nBear2, new2, hc2] = htfSlot(eTf2, eUse2, zH2, 2, evKey, evTxt)
[v3, t3, f3, nBull3, nBear3, new3, hc3] = htfSlot(eTf3, eUse3, zH3, 3, evKey, evTxt)
[v4, t4, f4, nBull4, nBear4, new4, hc4] = htfSlot(eTf4, eUse4, zH4, 4, evKey, evTxt)
[v5, t5, f5, nBull5, nBear5, new5, hc5] = htfSlot(eTf5, eUse5, zH5, 5, evKey, evTxt)

// HTF mitigation after creation: the chart bar an HTF zone appears on already counts (it comes after the HTF bar
// that formed the zone), and OBs in Close mode need a close of their own timeframe beyond the zone
if barstate.isconfirmed
    updateZones(zH1, new1, hc1)
    updateZones(zH2, new2, hc2)
    updateZones(zH3, new3, hc3)
    updateZones(zH4, new4, hc4)
    updateZones(zH5, new5, hc5)

// Price entering a zone (every tick on realtime bars -> notification as soon as price reaches the zone)
[eb0, es0] = checkEntry(zC, evKey, evTxt)
[eb1, es1] = checkEntry(zH1, evKey, evTxt)
[eb2, es2] = checkEntry(zH2, evKey, evTxt)
[eb3, es3] = checkEntry(zH3, evKey, evTxt)
[eb4, es4] = checkEntry(zH4, evKey, evTxt)
[eb5, es5] = checkEntry(zH5, evKey, evTxt)
bool enterBull = eb0 or eb1 or eb2 or eb3 or eb4 or eb5
bool enterBear = es0 or es1 or es2 or es3 or es4 or es5

// Price approaching a 1H / 4H / 1D zone (heads-up before it gets there)
if alNear
    checkNear(zC, evKey, evTxt)
    checkNear(zH1, evKey, evTxt)
    checkNear(zH2, evKey, evTxt)
    checkNear(zH3, evKey, evTxt)
    checkNear(zH4, evKey, evTxt)
    checkNear(zH5, evKey, evTxt)

// 1H / 4H trend change
string trendMsg = joinMsg(joinMsg(trendFlipMsg(eTf1, v1, t1, f1), trendFlipMsg(eTf2, v2, t2, f2)),
     joinMsg(trendFlipMsg(eTf3, v3, t3, f3), joinMsg(trendFlipMsg(eTf4, v4, t4, f4), trendFlipMsg(eTf5, v5, t5, f5))))
if alTrend and trendMsg != ""
    pushEv(evKey, evTxt, "T", trendMsg)

//==============================================================================
// LIQUIDITY (PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL, Asia range, equal highs / lows) + sweep markers
//==============================================================================
type Liq
    line   ln
    label  lb
    float  price
    bool   up        // true = buy-side liquidity (above highs), false = sell-side (below lows)
    string name
    int    born
    bool   eq
    bool   done = false

var array<Liq> liqs = array.new<Liq>()
bool   liqOn  = showLiq and timeframe.isintraday
color  liqLn  = color.new(liqCol, 15)
color  liqTx  = liqCol

dropLiq(int i) =>
    Liq q = liqs.remove(i)
    q.ln.delete()
    q.lb.delete()

newLiq(float price, int t, bool up, string name, bool eq) =>
    line  ln = line.new(t, price, time, price, xloc = xloc.bar_time, extend = extend.right, color = liqLn, style = line.style_dotted)
    label lb = label.new(time, price, name, xloc = xloc.bar_time, style = label.style_label_left, color = color(na), textcolor = liqTx, size = size.tiny)
    liqs.push(Liq.new(ln, lb, price, up, name, bar_index, eq))
    // Keep the drawing budget: oldest finished levels first, then the oldest active EQ levels beyond maxEq
    int nEq = 0
    for q in liqs
        nEq += (q.eq and not q.done) ? 1 : 0
    while liqs.size() > 40 or nEq > maxEq
        int k = -1
        for j = 0 to liqs.size() - 1
            Liq c = liqs.get(j)
            if c.done or (nEq > maxEq and c.eq)
                k := j
                break
        if k < 0
            break
        nEq -= (liqs.get(k).eq and not liqs.get(k).done) ? 1 : 0
        dropLiq(k)

// Remove still-active levels with this name (a new session / day replaces them)
expireLiq(string name) =>
    int n = liqs.size()
    if n > 0
        for i = n - 1 to 0
            Liq q = liqs.get(i)
            if not q.done and q.name == name
                dropLiq(i)

// Equal highs / lows from chart-TF swings
float eph = ta.pivothigh(high, eqLen, eqLen)
float epl = ta.pivotlow(low, eqLen, eqLen)
var array<float> eqHp = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   eqHt = array.new<int>()
var array<float> eqLp = array.new<float>()
var array<int>   eqLt = array.new<int>()

// Session sources
[pdh, pdl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "D", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
[pwh, pwl] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, "W", [high[1], low[1]], lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
bool  newDayL  = timeframe.change("D")
bool  newWeekL = timeframe.change("W")
bool  inAsia   = not na(time(timeframe.period, asiaSess, "UTC"))
var float asiaH = na
var float asiaL = na
var int   asiaT = na

string bslHit = ""   // buy-side levels swept this bar (wick above, close back below)
string sslHit = ""   // sell-side levels swept this bar (wick below, close back above)
if liqOn and barstate.isconfirmed
    // 1) Daily / weekly levels
    if liqPD and newDayL and not na(pdh)
        expireLiq("PDH")
        expireLiq("PDL")
        newLiq(pdh, time, true, "PDH", false)
        newLiq(pdl, time, false, "PDL", false)
    if liqPW and newWeekL and not na(pwh)
        expireLiq("PWH")
        expireLiq("PWL")
        newLiq(pwh, time, true, "PWH", false)
        newLiq(pwl, time, false, "PWL", false)
    // 2) Asian range: track during the session, publish when it ends
    if liqAsia
        if inAsia and not inAsia[1]
            asiaH := high
            asiaL := low
            asiaT := time
        else if inAsia
            asiaH := math.max(asiaH, high)
            asiaL := math.min(asiaL, low)
        if not inAsia and inAsia[1] and not na(asiaH)
            expireLiq("Asia H")
            expireLiq("Asia L")
            newLiq(asiaH, asiaT, true, "Asia H", false)
            newLiq(asiaL, asiaT, false, "Asia L", false)
    // 3) Equal highs / lows: a new swing within tolerance of an earlier unswept swing
    if liqEq
        float tol = eqTol * atrC
        int nh = eqHp.size()
        if nh > 0
            for j = nh - 1 to 0
                if high > eqHp.get(j)
                    eqHp.remove(j)
                    eqHt.remove(j)
        int nl = eqLp.size()
        if nl > 0
            for j = nl - 1 to 0
                if low < eqLp.get(j)
                    eqLp.remove(j)
                    eqLt.remove(j)
        if not na(eph)
            int m = eqHp.size()
            if m > 0
                for j = m - 1 to 0
                    if math.abs(eqHp.get(j) - eph) <= tol
                        float lvl = math.max(eqHp.get(j), eph)
                        bool  dup = false
                        for q in liqs
                            dup := dup or (not q.done and q.up and q.eq and math.abs(q.price - lvl) <= tol)
                        if not dup
                            newLiq(lvl, eqHt.get(j), true, "EQH", true)
                        break
            eqHp.push(eph)
            eqHt.push(time[eqLen])
            if eqHp.size() > 20
                eqHp.shift()
                eqHt.shift()
        if not na(epl)
            int m = eqLp.size()
            if m > 0
                for j = m - 1 to 0
                    if math.abs(eqLp.get(j) - epl) <= tol
                        float lvl = math.min(eqLp.get(j), epl)
                        bool  dup = false
                        for q in liqs
                            dup := dup or (not q.done and not q.up and q.eq and math.abs(q.price - lvl) <= tol)
                        if not dup
                            newLiq(lvl, eqLt.get(j), false, "EQL", true)
                        break
            eqLp.push(epl)
            eqLt.push(time[eqLen])
            if eqLp.size() > 20
                eqLp.shift()
                eqLt.shift()
    // 4) Sweeps / breaks, after the new levels above: the first bar after the Asian session or a new day
    //    (e.g. London open taking the Asia high) is checked against the levels it just received
    for q in liqs
        if not q.done and bar_index >= q.born and (q.up ? high > q.price : low < q.price)
            bool grab = q.up ? close < q.price : close > q.price
            q.done := true
            q.ln.set_extend(extend.none)
            q.ln.set_x2(time)
            q.ln.set_color(color.new(liqCol, 65))
            q.lb.delete()     // keep only the faded line; the $ marker tooltip names the level
            if grab and q.up
                bslHit := bslHit == "" ? q.name : bslHit + ", " + q.name
            if grab and not q.up
                sslHit := sslHit == "" ? q.name : sslHit + ", " + q.name
    // 5) Sweep markers
    if bslHit != "" and histOk
        histLabels.push(label.new(time, high, "$", xloc = xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.abovebar, style = label.style_none, textcolor = liqCol,
             size = size.small, tooltip = "Buy-side liquidity swept: " + bslHit))
    if bslHit != "" and alLiq
        pushEv(evKey, evTxt, "LB", "swept buy-side liquidity (" + bslHit + ") @ " + fmt(high))
    if sslHit != "" and histOk
        histLabels.push(label.new(time, low, "$", xloc = xloc.bar_time, yloc = yloc.belowbar, style = label.style_none, textcolor = liqCol,
             size = size.small, tooltip = "Sell-side liquidity swept: " + sslHit))
    if sslHit != "" and alLiq
        pushEv(evKey, evTxt, "LS", "swept sell-side liquidity (" + sslHit + ") @ " + fmt(low))

if barstate.islast
    refreshDisplay()
    if histDays > 0
        while histLines.size() > 0 and histLines.first().get_x2() < histCut
            line.delete(histLines.shift())
        while histLabels.size() > 0 and histLabels.first().get_x() < histCut
            label.delete(histLabels.shift())
        int nl = liqs.size()
        if nl > 0
            for i = nl - 1 to 0
                Liq lq = liqs.get(i)
                if lq.done and lq.ln.get_x2() < histCut
                    dropLiq(i)
    array<Liq> act = array.new<Liq>()
    for q in liqs
        if not q.done
            q.lb.set_x(time + 3 * chartSec * 1000)
            q.lb.set_text(q.name)
            act.push(q)
    int na2 = act.size()
    if na2 > 1
        for i = 0 to na2 - 2
            Liq a = act.get(i)
            if a.lb.get_text() != ""
                for j = i + 1 to na2 - 1
                    Liq b = act.get(j)
                    if b.lb.get_text() != "" and math.abs(a.price - b.price) < 0.15 * atrC
                        a.lb.set_text(a.lb.get_text() + " · " + b.name)
                        b.lb.set_text("")

// Market structure (BOS / CHoCH): chart timeframe, or a higher one (Auto: 15m on charts of 5m and below)
string msTfReq = msTfOpt == "15m" ? "15" : msTfOpt == "1H" ? "60" : msTfOpt == "Auto" and chartS <= 300 ? "15" : timeframe.period
bool   msHtf   = timeframe.in_seconds(msTfReq) > chartS
string msTf    = msHtf ? msTfReq : timeframe.period
[hms, hmsLvl, hmsX] = request.security(syminfo.tickerid, msTf, structConfirmed(swingLen), lookahead = barmerge.lookahead_on)
bool   msNew = timeframe.change(msTf)
int    sMs   = msHtf ? (msNew ? hms : 0) : (barstate.isconfirmed ? cms : 0)
float  sLvl  = msHtf ? hmsLvl : cmsLvl
int    sX    = msHtf ? hmsX : cmsX
bool msShow = msMode == "All" ? sMs != 0 : msMode == "CHoCH only" ? math.abs(sMs) == 2 : false
if msShow
    color  c   = sMs > 0 ? msBullCol : msBearCol
    string txt = (math.abs(sMs) == 2 ? "CHoCH" : "BOS") + (msHtf ? " " + tfName(msTf) : "")
    if histOk
        histLines.push(line.new(sX, sLvl, time, sLvl, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c, style = line.style_dashed))
        histLabels.push(label.new(int(math.avg(sX, time)), sLvl, txt, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color(na), textcolor = c,
             style = sMs > 0 ? label.style_label_down : label.style_label_up, size = size.tiny))
    if alMS
        pushEv(evKey, evTxt, "M", (sMs > 0 ? "Bullish " : "Bearish ") + txt + " @ " + fmt(sLvl))

//==============================================================================
// RSI DIVERGENCE (regular, chart timeframe)
//==============================================================================
// A new price pivot is measured against the most extreme earlier pivot of the same side within divMax bars
// (not just the previous one, so small swings in between do not hide a divergence):
// lower low + higher RSI = bullish, higher high + lower RSI = bearish
type Piv
    float price
    float rsi
    int   t
    int   b

float rsiV  = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
float divPL = ta.pivotlow(low, divL, divR)
float divPH = ta.pivothigh(high, divL, divR)
var array<Piv> divLows  = array.new<Piv>()
var array<Piv> divHighs = array.new<Piv>()

// Lowest (low = true) or highest earlier pivot that is 5..divMax bars before bar b
divRef(array<Piv> ps, int b, bool low) =>
    Piv ref = na
    for p in ps
        int gap = b - p.b
        if gap >= 5 and gap <= divMax and (na(ref) or (low ? p.price < ref.price : p.price > ref.price))
            ref := p
    ref

// Keep the pivot and forget the ones too old to pair with later pivots
divKeep(array<Piv> ps, Piv p) =>
    ps.push(p)
    while ps.size() > 0 and p.b - ps.first().b > divMax
        ps.shift()

drawDiv(int t1, float p1, int t2, float p2, bool bull, string tip) =>
    color c = bull ? msBullCol : msBearCol
    histLines.push(line.new(t1, p1, t2, p2, xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = c, width = 2))
    histLabels.push(label.new(t2, p2, bull ? "Bull Div" : "Bear Div", xloc = xloc.bar_time, color = color(na), textcolor = c,
         style = bull ? label.style_label_up : label.style_label_down, size = size.tiny, tooltip = tip))

bool bullDiv = false
bool bearDiv = false
string divMsg = ""
if showDiv and barstate.isconfirmed
    int pb = bar_index - divR
    int pt = time[divR]
    float pr = rsiV[divR]
    if not na(divPL)
        Piv ref = divRef(divLows, pb, true)
        if not na(ref) and divPL < ref.price and pr > ref.rsi and (not divZone or ref.rsi <= divLo)
            bullDiv := true
            divMsg  := "Bullish RSI divergence: price " + fmt(ref.price) + " → " + fmt(divPL) + ", RSI " + str.tostring(ref.rsi, "#.0") + " → " + str.tostring(pr, "#.0")
            if histOk
                drawDiv(ref.t, ref.price, pt, divPL, true, divMsg)
        divKeep(divLows, Piv.new(divPL, pr, pt, pb))
    if not na(divPH)
        Piv ref = divRef(divHighs, pb, false)
        if not na(ref) and divPH > ref.price and pr < ref.rsi and (not divZone or ref.rsi >= divHi)
            bearDiv := true
            string bm = "Bearish RSI divergence: price " + fmt(ref.price) + " → " + fmt(divPH) + ", RSI " + str.tostring(ref.rsi, "#.0") + " → " + str.tostring(pr, "#.0")
            divMsg  := joinMsg(divMsg, bm)
            if histOk
                drawDiv(ref.t, ref.price, pt, divPH, false, bm)
        divKeep(divHighs, Piv.new(divPH, pr, pt, pb))
    if alDiv and divMsg != ""
        pushEv(evKey, evTxt, "D", divMsg)

//==============================================================================
// NOTIFICATIONS: one alert() with every new event of this update
//==============================================================================
// alert.freq_all + a per-bar list of events already sent: each event reaches the phone exactly once, also when
// several happen in the same bar (with alert.freq_once_per_bar only the first alert of a bar got through, so
// e.g. a second zone entered a minute later in the same 5m bar was never notified)
varip int    sentBar  = -1
varip string sentKeys = ""
if sentBar != bar_index
    sentBar  := bar_index
    sentKeys := ""
string outMsg = ""
for [i, k] in evKey
    if not str.contains(sentKeys, "#" + k + "#")
        sentKeys := sentKeys + "#" + k + "#"
        outMsg   := joinMsg(outMsg, evTxt.get(i))
if outMsg != ""
    alert(syminfo.ticker + " " + fmt(close) + " " + outMsg, alert.freq_all)

//==============================================================================
// ALERT CONDITIONS
//==============================================================================
bool anyBull = cnb or cnbf or nBull1 or nBull2 or nBull3 or nBull4 or nBull5
bool anyBear = cns or cnsf or nBear1 or nBear2 or nBear3 or nBear4 or nBear5
alertcondition(anyBull, "New Bullish OB/FVG (any TF)", "{{ticker}} new Bullish Order Block / FVG")
alertcondition(anyBear, "New Bearish OB/FVG (any TF)", "{{ticker}} new Bearish Order Block / FVG")
alertcondition(enterBull, "Price entered Bullish OB/FVG", "{{ticker}} price entered a Bullish OB/FVG zone @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(enterBear, "Price entered Bearish OB/FVG", "{{ticker}} price entered a Bearish OB/FVG zone @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(bslHit != "", "Buy-side liquidity swept", "{{ticker}} swept buy-side liquidity (highs) @ {{high}}")
alertcondition(sslHit != "", "Sell-side liquidity swept", "{{ticker}} swept sell-side liquidity (lows) @ {{low}}")
alertcondition(msShow and sMs > 0, "Bullish BOS/CHoCH", "{{ticker}} Bullish structure break @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(msShow and sMs < 0, "Bearish BOS/CHoCH", "{{ticker}} Bearish structure break @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(bullDiv, "Bullish RSI divergence", "{{ticker}} Bullish RSI divergence @ {{close}}")
alertcondition(bearDiv, "Bearish RSI divergence", "{{ticker}} Bearish RSI divergence @ {{close}}")

//==============================================================================
// DASHBOARD
//==============================================================================
// Compact: one row of "5m ▼" cells (flip level below), Full: TF / Trend / Flip table (k = position of the TF, 0 = chart TF)
trendCell(table tb, int k, string name, int tr, float flip, bool compact) =>
    string arrow = tr > 0 ? "▲" : tr < 0 ? "▼" : "–"
    string word  = tr > 0 ? "Bullish" : tr < 0 ? "Bearish" : "Neutral"
    color  c     = tr > 0 ? msBullCol : tr < 0 ? msBearCol : color.gray
    bool   hasF  = tr != 0 and not na(flip)
    string fTxt  = hasF ? (tr > 0 ? "< " : "> ") + fmtS(flip) : "–"
    string fDist = hasF ? " (" + (flip >= close ? "+" : "") + fmtS(flip - close) + ")" : ""
    string fTip  = hasF ? "Close " + (tr > 0 ? "below " : "above ") + fmtS(flip) + " turns " + name + (tr > 0 ? " Bearish" : " Bullish") + fDist :
         "No new swing yet to turn the " + name + " trend"
    if compact
        tb.cell(k, 0, name + " " + arrow, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(c, 20), text_size = size.small,
             tooltip = name + " trend: " + word)
        if dashFlip
            tb.cell(k, 1, fTxt, text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.tiny, tooltip = fTip)
    else
        tb.cell(0, k + 1, name + (k == 0 ? " (chart)" : ""), text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
        tb.cell(1, k + 1, arrow + " " + word, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = color.new(c, 20), text_size = size.small)
        if dashFlip
            tb.cell(2, k + 1, fTxt + fDist, text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small, tooltip = fTip)

if showDash and barstate.islast
    string p = dashPos == "Top Right" ? position.top_right : dashPos == "Bottom Right" ? position.bottom_right :
         dashPos == "Top Left" ? position.top_left : position.bottom_left
    bool cmp = dashStyle == "Compact"
    var table tb = table.new(p, 6, 7, bgcolor = color.new(chart.bg_color, 10), border_color = color.new(chart.fg_color, 80),
         border_width = 1, frame_color = color.new(chart.fg_color, 70), frame_width = 1)
    tb.clear(0, 0, 5, 6)
    if not cmp
        tb.cell(0, 0, "TF", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
        tb.cell(1, 0, "Trend", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
        if dashFlip
            tb.cell(2, 0, "Flip at", text_color = chart.fg_color, text_size = size.small)
    int k = 0
    trendCell(tb, k, chartTag, cTrend, cFlip, cmp)
    if v1
        k += 1
        trendCell(tb, k, tfName(eTf1), t1, f1, cmp)
    if v2
        k += 1
        trendCell(tb, k, tfName(eTf2), t2, f2, cmp)
    if v3
        k += 1
        trendCell(tb, k, tfName(eTf3), t3, f3, cmp)
    if v4
        k += 1
        trendCell(tb, k, tfName(eTf4), t4, f4, cmp)
    if v5
        k += 1
        trendCell(tb, k, tfName(eTf5), t5, f5, cmp)
